  "Number": 40,
  "Question": "Given \\(a_0=1,\\) \\(a_1=3,\\) and the general relation \\(a_n^2-a_{n-1}a_{n+1}=(-1)^n\\) for \\(n\\ge1.\\) Then \\(a_3\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{13}{27}\\)",
    "B": "\\(33\\)",
    "C": "\\(21\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(-17\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The relation connects three consecutive terms. Use \\(n=1\\) first to find \\(a_2\\), then \\(n=2\\) to find \\(a_3\\).\n\nFor \\(n=1\\), the given values give\n\\[\n3^2-1\\cdot a_2=(-1)^1=-1.\n\\]\nThus \\(9-a_2=-1\\), so \\(a_2=10\\).\n\nFor \\(n=2\\), we now have\n\\[\n10^2-3a_3=(-1)^2=1.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(3a_3=99\\), and division by the nonzero coefficient \\(3\\) gives \\(\\boxed{a_3=33}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
